l inspection of skin lesions as part of diagnostic evaluation. This indicates that, at least for some cancers/lesions, physical examination is an enumerated component of the diagnostic workup alongside other tests. [Data: Entities (377); Relationships (508)]\\n\\nThe network also ties DIAGNOSIS to DRE as recommended testing after an anal cancer diagnosis, illustrating how the diagnostic milestone can trigger specific follow-on evaluations. [Data: Entities (6101); Relationships (13981)]\"},{\"summary\":\"The community encodes a formal diagnostic criterion for ALL while acknowledging possible exceptions\",\"explanation\":\"A defined diagnostic threshold appears as a node: DIAGNOSTIC THRESHOLD (20% LYMPHOBLASTS), described as a general criterion for ALL diagnosis (20% or more lymphoblasts in the bone marrow), with a note that certain cases may be diagnosed with less. [Data: Entities (3060)]\\n\\nThis criterion is explicitly connected to DIAGNOSIS, indicating that the community includes not only procedures but also rule-like decision thresholds used to establish or classify disease. [Data: Relationships (6036); Entities (15, 3060)]\"},{\"summary\":\"Presentation at first diagnosis can already be advanced disease (de novo stage IV metastatic breast cancer)\",\"explanation\":\"The entity DE NOVO STAGE IV METASTATIC BREAST CANCER captures a scenario where the first diagnosis is already stage IV metastatic disease rather than progression from earlier stages. [Data: Entities (3897)]\\n\\nA relationship links this concept directly to DIAGNOSIS, underscoring that staging and extent at the time of initial confirmation can be a defining feature of the clinical situation described by this community. [Data: Relationships (8161); Entities (15, 3897)]\"},{\"summary\":\"Differential diagnosis is emphasized where symptoms can mimic primary CNS lymphoma\",\"explanation\":\"The community contains two entities—NEUROLOGICAL ILLNESSES and OTHER TYPES OF BRAIN CANCER—described as categories